// The world the `bram` sample builds against.
//
// Like andy, it exports nothing but the player data plane. Bram is written in
// C# and compiled to a WASI 0.2.3 reactor component with componentize-dotnet
// (NativeAOT-LLVM + WASI SDK). The .NET runtime lowers the BCL onto the WASI 0.2
// imports automatically:
//
//   * Console.WriteLine        -> wasi:cli/stdout (Bram's guild-boss rallies)
//   * System.IO.File           -> wasi:filesystem (his roster + tax ledger)
//   * DateTime / Environment    -> wasi:clocks, wasi:cli/environment
//
// So those imports don't need to be declared here — NativeAOT-LLVM contributes
// the WASI import world and the component encoder merges it with the `player`
// export world emitted by `wit-bindgen c-sharp`. Keeping the bindgen world to
// just the interface we implement mirrors how andy builds.
package better-together:bram@0.1.0;

/// A single Bram player component: a WASI 0.2.3 reactor that exports the
/// Better Together player interface.
world bram {
    export better-together:gardener/player@0.1.0;
}
